; err_trace for Melange.
;
; vendored/err_trace ships a melange stanza of its own, but it is unusable here:
; it is gated on ERR_TRACE_TEST_MELANGE=true, and that same env var DISABLES the
; ordinary src/ library. Enabling one would turn the other off, so the native
; build and the melange build could never both work in one tree.
;
; So mirror the source instead, exactly as js/melange/core does for lib/core:
; copied, never forked, so a change upstream cannot leave the melange build
; testing older code than the native golden.
;
; [wrapped false] so the module is [Err], the same name lib/core uses natively.
; The library name differs from the cross-project [err_trace] so the two can
; never collide.
;
; Vendored source: its warnings are upstream's business, and dev profile would
; otherwise fail the build on them -- same rule as js/melange/vendor/fmt.

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/vendored/err_trace/src/err.{ml,mli}))

(library
 (name err_trace_mel)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes melange)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{profile} melange))
 (flags
  (:standard -w -a)))
